<title>CHINA: Shanghai metal exchange to extend trading hours.</title>
<headline>Shanghai metal exchange to extend trading hours.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Metal Exchange will extend trading hours for copper and aluminium contracts as from next Monday, exchange officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The revisions were ordered by the China Securities Regulatory Commission who wants all China's five futures exchanges with metal contracts to trade during the same period, one official said.</p>
<p>Following is the new timetable: (as from November 18, in local times, eight hours ahead of GMT)</p>
<p>    AM  0900 - 0940	Copper, Aluminium</p>
<p>	  0945 - 1015	Copper, Aluminium</p>
<p>	  1030 - 1055	Zinc, Lead, Tin, Nickel</p>
<p>	  1100 - 1130	Copper, Aluminium</p>
<p>    PM  1330 - 1410	Aluminium</p>
<p>	  1420 - 1500	Copper</p>
<p>Following is the timetable from June 3, 1996 to November 15, 1996:</p>
<p>    AM  0850 - 0930	Copper, Aluminium</p>
<p>	  0935 - 1015	Copper, Aluminium</p>
<p>	  1030 - 1100	Zinc, Lead, Tin, Nickel</p>
<p>	  1105 - 1145	Copper, Aluminium</p>
</text>
